WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.290 --> 00:00:09.030
President Joe Biden has proposed raising
the corporate income tax rate

00:00:09.030 --> 00:00:13.679
from 21% to 28%. The rate increase would raise more than

00:00:13.679 --> 00:00:17.680
$700 billion in additional
revenue over the next decade

00:00:17.680 --> 00:00:22.240
to help finance his American Jobs Plan.
A higher corporate tax rate will help

00:00:22.240 --> 00:00:25.856
finance new spending, but it will come at a cost.

00:00:25.856 --> 00:00:31.193
A higher corporate rate increases the incentive
to shift profits out of the United States.

00:00:31.193 --> 00:00:34.320
Under Biden's proposal, the US corporate tax rate,

00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:38.640
including state and local taxes, would be roughly 32%

00:00:38.640 --> 00:00:43.520
and the highest among OECD nations. This
will make it more attractive to locate

00:00:43.520 --> 00:00:48.320
income in foreign jurisdictions.
A higher corporate tax rate would also

00:00:48.320 --> 00:00:52.985
make investing in the United States
more expensive. A higher tax burden

00:00:52.985 --> 00:00:56.160
on investment can lead to a smaller capital stock,

00:00:56.160 --> 00:01:00.879
lower labor productivity, and lower
economic output in the long run.

00:01:00.879 --> 00:01:05.040
To the extent that a corporate tax rate
reduces labor productivity,

00:01:05.040 --> 00:01:08.880
it will lead to lower wages for everyday workers.

00:01:08.880 --> 00:01:12.000
How high do you think the corporate tax
rate should be?

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:16.400
Let us know in our poll. Also, let us know
what other topics you'd like our

00:01:16.400 --> 00:01:20.640
scholars to cover in 60 seconds,
and be sure to LIKE and subscribe for

00:01:20.640 --> 00:01:25.439
more research and videos from AEI.

